course: dictionary
lesson: 1766
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning is right. «In New York, Clementine's parents miss her school play because of a work trip.» Clementine has a capital letter, and it is someone who has parents and goes to school, so Clementine must be a girl's name.
explain: Now read this: «Peel a clementine and share it with your friend.» There is no capital letter and you can peel it, so a clementine here is a fruit. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A small, sweet orange fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Capital letters are clues. A name always starts with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence. A fruit does not. When you meet a word with two meanings, check the capital letter, then check the words around it, then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: A clementine is a small, sweet orange fruit that is easy to peel.
fact: A clementine usually has no seeds, so it is a popular fruit for lunchboxes, especially in the UK.
fact: «Clementine» with a capital C is a girl's name, as in the old song "Oh My Darling, Clementine".
fact: The plural of clementine is clementines, as in «a bag of clementines».
fact: Capital letters and the words around a word are clues to its meaning.
exercise: «Peel a clementine before you eat it.» What is a clementine? | *A small, sweet orange fruit | A large green vegetable | A type of school lesson | A bird that sings in the morning
exercise: «In New York, Clementine's parents send flowers.» Is Clementine a fruit or a girl? | A city in America | *A girl | A fruit | A type of cake
exercise: A clementine is easy to peel and usually has no seeds. What does usually tell you? | It is very large | It is always sour | It always has seeds | *Most of the time it has no seeds
test: «Dad helps me peel a clementine, and the peel comes off in one piece.» What does peel mean here? | *To take the skin off | To shout loudly | To count out loud | To paint a wall
test: What is the plural of clementine, as in «a bag of clementines»? | *clementines | clementinees | clementine's | clementinies
exam: «Clementine's parents miss her school play, so they send flowers and a video call.» Why does the author write Clementine with a capital C? | It is the start of a sentence | *It is a girl's name | It is a fruit | It is the name of a school
